    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_20b1cb014a6c9a1deacbe9f7968b593f8abbefdeef3ab1068bf815752eb388f4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source factors the zeta crossover into components with different provenance: Haar-unitary calculations supply the Barnes-G normalization and the Bessel crossover F_k, while the zeta conjecture appends the prime-dependent Euler-product factor a(k). Agreement at k=1 and algebraic agreement with the shortened k=2 number-theoretic calculation calibrate this factorization without promoting the general or endpoint formulas to theorems.",
