    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f07f155ce2c2b33489cd419e8695a77d0e33f4de173e341be624fbca9b66eda1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The same density-scaled displacement links two genuinely different source layers: Theorem 3 proves for Haar-unitary characteristic polynomials that the Bessel factor F_k moves from zero-sensitive scaling to F_k→1, while Conjecture 5 transfers that factor to zeta so that the α→0 regime conditionally yields derivative moments and the growing scaled-offset regime is intended to yield ordinary-moment behavior in a discrete mean.",
